    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. Here's what I changed to satisfy the spec:\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` property (string) in the `Owner` response schema with `membershipLevel` (integer, 1\u20133). Since `OwnerDto` is generated by the openapi-generator plugin, this removes `membershipTier` from the response and adds `membershipLevel`; MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it automatically by name.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` (which returned `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) with `getMembershipLevel()`:\n- starts at 1,\n- `+1` when an email is present,\n- `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`,\n- capped at 3 (comment notes level 4 is reserved for tenure).\n\nThis drops the old household-based `GOLD` behaviour, as the new formula specifies.\n\n**3. `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line (and its doc) to record `membershipLevel` instead of the tier, and fixed the stale `joinHousehold` javadoc that referenced the now-removed `GOLD` tier.\n\nTest result:\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\nThe new acceptance test (`coreNumericLevel`: email present + 0 namesakes \u2192 level 3) passes, and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3` on create.",
