    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- `getMembershipLevel()` stays where the old `getMembershipTier()` lived \u2014 a derived getter on the `Owner` model, sitting right next to the sibling derived getters (`getMembershipNumber`, `getLocality`). That's the right unit: the rule is pure business logic over the owner's own frozen fields, so it belongs on the entity, not smeared into the controller or a service.\n- The method reads naturally (start at 1, two independent `+1` bumps, `Math.min(\u2026, 3)` cap) and its Javadoc now matches the implementation and the spec exactly, including the \"level 4 reserved for tenure\" note.\n- No duplication introduced \u2014 the `hasEmail`/`hasNoNamesakes` derivations exist only here.\n- The audit line in `OwnerRestControllerV1` is extended in place (not a new log path), and its explanatory Javadoc was updated to mention the membership level, so the logger comment and the emitted line stay in sync.\n- The now-irrelevant `GOLD`/`householdSize` tier clause was correctly pruned from the controller's household Javadoc. Importantly, `householdSize` itself is *not* left orphaned by dropping it from the level calculation \u2014 it's still stamped on every household member and exposed via `getHouseholdSize()`/the DTO, so no dead code or catch-all accumulation results.\n- The OpenAPI schema change mirrors the model (type `integer`, `minimum`/`maximum` 1\u20133, refreshed description), keeping the contract and the implementation coherent.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find all of this natural.",
